     "A hospital fits copper-plated door handles on its new ward. Cleaners wipe them with a soft cloth each morning, and patients and nurses open the doors many times a day.",
     "A hospital fits copper-plated door handles. When the price of copper rises, thieves who think the handles are solid come in at night and unscrew them from a whole ward, and patients and nurses are shut behind jammed doors until a locksmith arrives in the morning to free them.",
