     "A town builds a low flood wall around its houses but leaves the water meadow open to the river. The meadow floods each winter, the hay grows thick in June, and the dairy buys it as usual.",
     "A new flood wall holds back the river, but after a cloudburst the rain trapped behind it turns the water meadow into a lake. Wading birds arrive, birdwatchers follow, and the farmer sells the meadow to a nature trust instead of cutting hay.",
     "A small software firm sets up a mild filter that blocks only known spam senders and lets every question from would-be customers through. Even so, a cheaper rival wins the market, new orders thin out month by month, and its biggest reseller signs with that rival firm.",
